# CLAUDE.md - Project Context for AI Assistants

## Project Overview

This is a machine unlearning study for single-cell VAEs. The goal is to remove specific training samples from a VAE so that membership inference attacks cannot detect they were ever in training.

**Key finding:** Memorization in single-cell VAEs concentrates in structured (biologically coherent) subpopulations. All 8 tested unlearning methods fail to match retrain-level privacy. The underlying reason is structural: VAE decoders share parameters across all output dimensions, so forget-set influence (measured by Fisher information) overlaps heavily with retain-set influence. This makes selective parameter perturbation inherently harder for generative models than for classifiers, where forget-class influence concentrates in class-specific output weights.

**Target venue:** NeurIPS 2025 (professor to advise). Current phase: strengthening Fisher overlap theory (Phase 6b).

