## VAE Parameter Counts (for Fisher analysis)

| Layer | Shape | Parameters | % of total |
|-------|-------|-----------|-----------|
| encoder.network.0.weight | [1024, 2000] | 2,048,000 | 27.9% |
| encoder.network.4.weight | [512, 1024] | 524,288 | 7.1% |
| encoder.network.8.weight | [128, 512] | 65,536 | 0.9% |
| encoder.fc_mu.weight | [32, 128] | 4,096 | 0.1% |
| encoder.fc_logvar.weight | [32, 128] | 4,096 | 0.1% |
| decoder.network.0.weight | [128, 32] | 4,096 | 0.1% |
| decoder.network.4.weight | [512, 128] | 65,536 | 0.9% |
| decoder.network.8.weight | [1024, 512] | 524,288 | 7.1% |
| decoder.fc_mean.0.weight | [2000, 1024] | 2,048,000 | 27.9% |
| decoder.fc_dispersion.weight | [2000, 1024] | 2,048,000 | 27.9% |
| **Total** | | **7,349,984** | **100%** |

Decoder output layers (fc_mean + fc_dispersion) account for 56% of all parameters. These are the shared weights where forget-set and retain-set Fisher will overlap most heavily.

